From: Stephender (Antigravity lead-planner proposal, Phase 1 Fix 3, v2 rework)
Subject: [PATCH] Return freed TBB allocator pools to the OS + guard huge pages on low-RAM systems

Fix 3 from ANTIGRAVITY-PLAN.md. Applies on top of 0001-undo-hardening +
0002-ram-aware-cache against Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1).

Blender links tbbmalloc_proxy on Linux and Windows x64 but never calls
scalable_allocation_command(TBBMALLOC_CLEAN_ALL_BUFFERS, nullptr) to
release idle allocator caches, so RSS stays high after a render, a file
load, or undo purges. This adds MEM_trim_unused() and calls it on cold
paths only: after undo steps are purged, at the end of
wm_file_read_post(), and at the end of RE_RenderFrame() / RE_RenderAnim().
It also gates Linux Transparent Huge Pages on >8 GiB physical RAM (was
unconditional).

Preserved corrections from v1:
1. Defines -DWITH_TBB_MALLOC and adds TBB include dirs in
   intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt (on Linux, WITH_TBB_MALLOC is
   otherwise only defined for source/creator/CMakeLists.txt:139-141).
2. Calls MEM_trim_unused() at the end of RE_RenderFrame()
   (pipeline.cc:1925..2009) and RE_RenderAnim() (pipeline.cc:2318..2612)
   since render_endjob() lives in editors/render/render_internal.cc, not
   pipeline.cc.

Changes vs v1 (rework):
1. Defect 1 (link failure on msgfmt and guardedalloc gtests) — fixed via
   Option (a): link `PRIVATE ${TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES}` directly in
   intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt under
   `if(WITH_TBB_MALLOC_PROXY AND TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES AND TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS)`.
   Why this links on BOTH Linux and Windows (traced in upstream v5.2.4):
   - Option & evaluation order: CMakeLists.txt:764-766 defines
     WITH_TBB_MALLOC_PROXY (default ON on Linux and Windows x64; unset on
     macOS and Windows ARM64). CMakeLists.txt:1542-1544 includes
     platform_unix / platform_win32 before add_subdirectory(intern) at
     CMakeLists.txt:2434, so TBB_* variables are already populated when
     intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt runs.
   - Linux: build_files/cmake/platform/platform_unix.cmake:499-511 sets
     TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS (line 505) and TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES from
     TBB::tbbmalloc LOCATION (line 509); line 520 calls
     add_bundled_libraries(tbb/lib), putting tbb/lib on LD_LIBRARY_PATH in
     PLATFORM_ENV_BUILD (platform_unix.cmake:1105-1109) for build-time
     tools like msgfmt (build_files/cmake/macros.cmake:1217).
   - Windows: CMakeLists.txt:1137 defaults WITH_WINDOWS_FIND_MODULES to
     OFF, so build_files/cmake/platform/platform_win32.cmake:779-810 takes
     the bundled-libs branch and sets TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS (line 802) and
     TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES (`optimized ${LIBDIR}/tbb/lib/tbbmalloc.lib
     debug ${LIBDIR}/tbb/lib/tbbmalloc_debug.lib`, lines 804-807).
     platform_win32.cmake:1209-1210 puts ${LIBDIR}/tbb/bin on PATH in
     PLATFORM_ENV_BUILD (for msgfmt) and line 1215 includes it in
     PLATFORM_ENV_INSTALL (for ctest).
   - CMake keyword handling & transitive link propagation:
     blender_add_lib() -> blender_link_libraries()
     (build_files/cmake/macros.cmake:395-424) explicitly parses PRIVATE,
     optimized, and debug tokens in LIB and defers bf::dependencies::*
     (pthreads) to the end, keeping tbbmalloc before pthreads. Because
     bf_intern_guardedalloc is a static library, CMake propagates its
     PRIVATE link libraries via $<LINK_ONLY:...> to every consumer,
     including targets without setup_platform_linker_libs() such as msgfmt
     (source/blender/blentranslation/msgfmt/CMakeLists.txt:22,36),
     guardedalloc_test (intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt:64, which also
     passes ${LIB} directly), and all gtests
     (build_files/cmake/testing.cmake:95).
   - Guard safety: checking `TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES AND TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS`
     ensures -DWITH_TBB_MALLOC is never defined without matching headers
     and link library (covering macOS, Windows ARM64, WITH_TBB=OFF,
     bpy_module/blender_lite, and non-default Windows builds with
     WITH_WINDOWS_FIND_MODULES=ON where platform_win32.cmake:781-789
     leaves TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES empty).
2. Defect 2 (header blast radius / ccache+sccache invalidation) — moved
   the MEM_trim_unused() declaration out of MEM_guardedalloc.h into a new
   dedicated header intern/guardedalloc/MEM_trim.h (listed in SRC in
   intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt) included ONLY by the 4 intended
   translation units: mallocn.cc, undo_system.cc, pipeline.cc, wm_files.cc.
   MEM_guardedalloc.h is completely untouched (byte-identical to upstream).
3. Bonus v1 bug fixed (CMake INC_SYS wipe + strict flags ordering):
   - In v1, `list(APPEND INC_SYS ${TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS})` ran at line 12 of
     intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt, BEFORE `set(INC_SYS )` at line
     17, which immediately cleared INC_SYS back to empty. Moved the block
     after `set(LIB ...)` (line 45) so both INC_SYS and LIB persist into
     blender_add_lib() and blender_add_test_suite_executable().
   - In intern/guardedalloc/intern/mallocn.cc, moved `#include "MEM_trim.h"`
     and `#include <tbb/scalable_allocator.h>` / `#include <malloc.h>`
     above `BLI_strict_flags.h` so third-party headers are not compiled
     under Blender's strict conversion/shadow error pragmas.
4. Bonus v1 bug fixed (Linux THP RAM check was a no-op):
   - BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes()
     (source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc:208-216) returns maximum
     addressable virtual memory (16 EiB on 64-bit), NOT physical RAM, so
     `> 8192` was always true. Replaced with POSIX `sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)`
     * `sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES)` under `#if defined(WITH_TBB_MALLOC) &&
     defined(__linux__)` (matching intern/cycles/util/system.cpp:262-264).

Remaining risks / still to verify in CI:
- Full Linux + Windows CI build & link (especially msgfmt, blender, and
  WITH_GTESTS=ON targets such as guardedalloc_test) has not been executed
  on this 6 GB VM (only mallocn.cc + MEM_trim.h + creator.cc sysconf
  syntax/symbol compile-checked with g++ -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Werror).
- Non-default Windows builds with -DWITH_WINDOWS_FIND_MODULES=ON do not
  populate TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES (platform_win32.cmake:781-789); the guard
  keeps them building cleanly, with MEM_trim_unused() as a no-op.
- Post-render, post-load, and post-undo-purge RSS benchmarks + zero
  render-time regression check remain to be measured after CI builds.

STATUS: STAGED (v2) - verified to apply cleanly on top of 0001 + 0002
against Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1). NOT yet in stephender-repo/patches/.

diff --git a/intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt b/intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt
index 2612f09..d001440 100644
--- a/intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/intern/guardedalloc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@ set(SRC
 
   MEM_guardedalloc.h
   MEM_safe_multiply.h
+  MEM_trim.h
   ./intern/mallocn_inline.hh
   ./intern/mallocn_intern.hh
   ./intern/mallocn_intern_function_pointers.hh
@@ -44,6 +45,16 @@ set(LIB
   PRIVATE bf::dependencies::pthreads
 )
 
+if(WITH_TBB_MALLOC_PROXY AND TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES AND TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS)
+  # MEM_trim_unused() calls scalable_allocation_command() directly in mallocn.cc.
+  # NOTE: On Linux, WITH_TBB_MALLOC is otherwise only defined for the creator target.
+  # Link TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES here so targets that link bf::intern::guardedalloc
+  # without setup_platform_linker_libs() (e.g. msgfmt, guardedalloc_test) also link cleanly.
+  add_definitions(-DWITH_TBB_MALLOC)
+  list(APPEND INC_SYS ${TBB_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+  list(APPEND LIB PRIVATE ${TBB_MALLOC_LIBRARIES})
+endif()
+
 blender_add_lib(bf_intern_guardedalloc "${SRC}" "${INC}" "${INC_SYS}" "${LIB}")
 add_library(bf::intern::guardedalloc ALIAS bf_intern_guardedalloc)
 
diff --git a/intern/guardedalloc/MEM_trim.h b/intern/guardedalloc/MEM_trim.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3965aa6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/intern/guardedalloc/MEM_trim.h
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+/* SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Blender Authors
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later */
+
+#pragma once
+
+/** \file
+ * \ingroup intern_mem
+ *
+ * Dedicated header for #MEM_trim_unused(), kept separate from `MEM_guardedalloc.h`
+ * so changes here do not invalidate compiler caches across the entire tree.
+ */
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+/**
+ * Return freed allocator pools to the OS (TBB allocator caches, or glibc
+ * malloc arenas). Call only on cold paths (after a render, a file load, or
+ * undo steps being purged) -- never in a hot loop.
+ */
+void MEM_trim_unused(void);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
diff --git a/intern/guardedalloc/intern/mallocn.cc b/intern/guardedalloc/intern/mallocn.cc
index 1de61c9..fdc8b9a 100644
--- a/intern/guardedalloc/intern/mallocn.cc
+++ b/intern/guardedalloc/intern/mallocn.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,13 @@
  */
 
 #include "MEM_guardedalloc.h"
+#include "MEM_trim.h"
+
+#ifdef WITH_TBB_MALLOC
+#  include <tbb/scalable_allocator.h>
+#elif defined(__GLIBC__)
+#  include <malloc.h>
+#endif
 
 /* To ensure strict conversions. */
 #include "../../source/blender/blenlib/BLI_strict_flags.h"
@@ -230,3 +237,13 @@ void MEM_use_guarded_allocator()
   MEM_name_ptr_set = MEM_guarded_name_ptr_set;
 #endif
 }
+
+void MEM_trim_unused()
+{
+#ifdef WITH_TBB_MALLOC
+  /* Release idle TBB allocator caches back to the OS. */
+  scalable_allocation_command(TBBMALLOC_CLEAN_ALL_BUFFERS, nullptr);
+#elif defined(__GLIBC__)
+  malloc_trim(0);
+#endif
+}
diff --git a/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/undo_system.cc b/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/undo_system.cc
index 235db21..de58e25 100644
--- a/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/undo_system.cc
+++ b/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/undo_system.cc
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include "RNA_access.hh"
 
 #include "MEM_guardedalloc.h"
+#include "MEM_trim.h"
 
 /* Header to pull symbols from the file which otherwise might get stripped away. */
 #include "BKE_blender_undo.hh"
@@ -488,6 +489,8 @@ void BKE_undosys_stack_limit_steps_and_memory(UndoStack *ustack, int steps, size
     /* Free from first to last, free functions may update de-duplication info
      * (see #MemFileUndoStep). */
     undosys_stack_clear_all_first(ustack, us_trim_last, us_exclude);
+    /* Return freed allocator pools to the OS now that undo steps are gone. */
+    MEM_trim_unused();
   }
 }
 
diff --git a/source/blender/render/intern/pipeline.cc b/source/blender/render/intern/pipeline.cc
